WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
International efforts to

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.068
Defuse tensions

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.702
in Kosovo

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.637
are stepping up as ethnic Serbs

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.139
held more protests today

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:06.639
in a town

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.375
where clashes broke out this week

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.010
between demonstrators

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.878
as well as native peacekeepers.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.879
NATO's sending

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.382
700 more troops to bolster its force.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.750
That we had that from Jens

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.784
Stoltenberg yesterday

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.586
after dozens were heard

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.855
amid the protests on Monday.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.290
The US responding by sidelining Kosovo

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.291
from joint NATO

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.127
exercises, blaming its leaders

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.462
for aggravating a tense situation

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.530
This is what France's

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.331
Emmanuel Macron

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.634
had to say, repeating Kosovo

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.702
incident.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.504
We have very clearly indicated

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.872
to Kosovar authorities

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.873
that it was a mistake

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.341
to proceed with these elections

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.143
in this type of context,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.077
which is an almost

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.979
complete nonparticipation.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.180
The Kosovar authorities

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.348
bear responsibility

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.216
for some of the current situation,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:50.784
and there was a

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.318
non respect of an agreement

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.219
that was important

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.020
and that was signed

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.355
only a couple of weeks ago.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.791
Well, Scott McClellan is

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:58.491
following the story

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.893
for us here in London. And Scott.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.694
Context is really important here.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.462
Before we talk about

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.030
what we've seen this week

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:04.864
and in previous weeks,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:05.432
just talk us

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.866
through the context of this region

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.968
that goes back decades. Of course, Yeah.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.736
So it's important to know

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.470
a bit of the history here.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.072
So Kosovo declared its independence

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.706
from Serbia in 2008.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.508
Many, many countries around the world,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.342
including the US.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.477
Many in Europe

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.711
recognized that independence

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.447
but Serbia did not.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.681
But it was a full one. Full.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.183
It doesn't recognize it from way up.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.284
From what I understand,

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.718
some important ones don't recognize it

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.853
in Russia.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:27.353
But what

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.354
I thought it was very interesting

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:28.955
what the president

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.690
actually told you last hour,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.624
which is that

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.926
it's not really a question anymore.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.828
So he's not explicitly acknowledging

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:35.361
the independence,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.830
but he's sort of in a roundabout way

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.731
saying, look, this is the reality.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.234
It's also important to know the ethnic

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.268
makeup of this region.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.871
So Kosovo is more than 90%

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.074
ethnic Albanian, with some exceptions.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.509
Including there's four

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.577
municipalities here.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.478
There's another smaller

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.313
one that's right about there

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.181
that a majority Serb in these regions

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.249
don't want to be ruled

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.984
by the powers that be in Kosovo.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.685
And this has caused

00:01:58.685 --> 00:01:59.586
all kinds of problems.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.019
So much

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.720
so that

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.354
ten years ago

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:05.325
2013 Kosovo and Serbia actually agreed on

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.025
this document

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.393
called the Brussels agreement,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.461
essentially gives

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.564
these regions some sort

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.198
of autonomy,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.833
something that President Verges told

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.568
you was still a major issue,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.003
that it wants

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.238
that it wants Kosovo

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.606
to actually implement.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.874
It gives them some autonomy

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.142
over education and health.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.309
It says that the police chief

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.644
should be an ethnic Serb

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.211
and that neither

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.980
Serbia and Kosovo will interfere

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:27.814
with each other's attempts

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.082
to join the E.U..

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.083
The problem is that

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:30.884
most of this

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:33.186
was never actually implemented, which,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.554
as the president pointed out,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.390
he blames the Kosovars because it's

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.626
mostly theirs to actually implement.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.995
And so that brings us to back in March,

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.830
Kosovo and Serbia agreed on this,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.031
which is sort of renewing

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:45.598
their commitment

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.100
to the Brussels agreement.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.601
And explicitly acknowledging that

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.536
if they can't figure out

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.670
how to actually implement

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.938
this, there will be consequences

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.740
from the European Union.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.608
But it hasn't been implemented.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:58.678
And that is why we have seen protests

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.713
in these northern parts of the country.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.681
Just talk us through

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.650
why they're so angry

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.951
in the north of Kosovo.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.085
Yeah.
And again, President Bush,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.855
which told you quite plainly that

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.791
these local elections were a big problem

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.393
because there there's legitimacy issue.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.194
So essentially

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:14.994
ethnic Serbs

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.063
in these northern municipalities

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.898
didn't vote in the local elections.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.333
By and large, they boycott it.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.534
And so you had voter turnout

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.604
that overall was 3.4%.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.538
And pretty piddly,

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.472
especially considering

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.308
when this municipality,

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.375
the mayor that was elected,

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.711
there only had 141 votes.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.579
There is obviously

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.314
a legitimacy question here,

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.182
which is why ethnic Serbs

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:36.749
in that area

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.052
protested, tried to block the mayors

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.887
from actually entering the town halls.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.622
This very violent protest,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.691
may I add, as well. Well, they got this.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.292
They were violent last week.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.294
But they got even more violent on Monday

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.763
when you had ethnic Serbs and

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.700
Naito peacekeeping forces clashes.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.034
There were explosions.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.370
There were some 30 Naito peacekeepers

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.171
who were injured.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.673
And yeah, this was a very ugly scene.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.676
They're all prompted by Kosovo's

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.377
insistence

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.179
on having these mayors

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.214
who don't have a lot of legitimacy

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.515
given the boycott of the vote,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.883
actually entering

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.385
these municipal offices.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.753
So we've heard

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.221
you heard a little clip from Macron

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.056
we heard from the NATO secretary general

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:17.790
as well,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.825
Jan Stoltenberg,

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.360
pealing calling for peace.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.262
Where does the US sign in all of this?

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.964
Yeah, they were quite plain about this.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.633
In blaming Kosovo,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.001
specifically the Kosovo prime

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.801
minister for this,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.304
and not responding to their requests

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.372
to de-escalate things.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.439
So this is what the ambassador

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.140
told journalists.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.408
He said this was a crisis

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.809
that from our perspective,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.044
was unnecessary.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.712
The operation that took place on Friday

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.814
to obtain access to municipal buildings

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.249
through forcible means

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.385
was not coordinated with the US.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.953
When we became aware of it,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.755
we advised strongly against it

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:51.724
because we anticipated consequences

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.059
that we are now seeing.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.360
And so is that there's two things

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.328
that the US

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.095
is expecting

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.930
from the Kosovo Prime Minister,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.831
and that is that

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.266
the mayors are not going to work

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.034
from the town hall.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.303
They want them to work at alternate sites

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.404
because they're largely doing

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.672
administrative work.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.706
But just on that,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:07.507
when I spoke to the Prime

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.374
Minister yesterday,

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.642
he did not sound like

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.710
he was going to budge on this

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.111
or in fact on this.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.446
Exactly, exactly.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:13.780
And so

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.147
and this is

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.382
despite pressure from the European Union

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.884
and the US, he was pretty defiant.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:18.384
Listen,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:22.188
I am working closely with

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.123
international factors

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.858
especially with the United States

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.293
and European Union.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.996
We consider both of them indispensable

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.265
allies, friends and partners.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.300
And we will do our best

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.403
but I am not surrendering democratic

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.872
republic to fascist militia.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.142
And so now you have the US

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.011
essentially canceling

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.179
Kosovo, its participation

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.213
in some military drills

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.915
that are actually taking place right now.

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:49.649
They're taking place over

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.951
two months in Romania.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:52.552
The ambassador

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.553
also explained that look, there's

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.321
not a whole lot of enthusiasm right now

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.122
on the United States

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.724
as part to advocate for Kosovo.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:58.257
It's one of its

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.459
most important allies,

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.961
if not its most important ally

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.296
when it comes to countries

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.832
that don't recognize their independence.

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:07.433
And they've made clear that, look,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.968
if they can't de-escalate

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:09.836
the situation,

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.003
there may be more consequences.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.338
And that is what is needed right now.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.806
The it needs to de-escalate.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.874
Scott, appreciate it.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:15.908
Thank you very much.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.910
Well, yesterday I spoke with Kosovo's

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.312
prime minister, Alban Curti.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:20.346
As you heard Scott mention

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.347
that you refer

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:22.982
to the protests as you had in that clip,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.751
a Serbian fascist,

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:26.586
and he accused Belgrade of stirring up

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:28.154
violent opposition to the elections.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:29.555
Well, in the last hour,

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:30.890
I put those claims to Serbia's

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.492
president, Aleksandar Vucic,

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.360
condemned Curtis's accusations

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.462
that he wants to stabilize the situation.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:36.996
Have a listen.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:39.966
We do regret the fact

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:41.300
that there were some major

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.169
soldiers injured,

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.204
and that's what we have publicly said.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.640
Immediately after it happened yesterday

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.541
and today

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.177
and you had them, we faced very peaceful.

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:54.180
We we faced very peaceful protests.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.415
And there were

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:58.951
physicians, nurses, teachers.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.320
Everybody was protesting

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.322
were those people blackmailed by someone?

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:04.690
Know those people?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.492
They just want to see

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:09.429
Kosovo special police forces withdrawing

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:11.631
from those premises.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.299
That has never, ever.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:15.902
We will talk about that, but also call it

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.004
legitimate and illegal measures as well.

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:19.939
You're calling for calm.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:23.309
Mr.
President, is that call for calm

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:24.710
also going to those

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.412
northern municipalities?

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.780
Do you have control

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.883
over those protesters?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.019
I don't have any kind of control,

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:36.055
but I believe that most of those people

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.491
will always show respect

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.625
to the state of Serbia.

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:43.262
And what we can do with our

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.532
international interlocutors,

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.835
with our partners

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:50.903
from European Union, United States,

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.940
all the others from all over the world

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.945
is that we need to have a stable region.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.380
Yeah. Why I'm saying that?

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.716
Because Serbia, when I say Serbia,

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:05.485
it means 50%

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.620
of overall Western Balkans economy.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:11.290
It means 63% of attracting

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.558
foreign direct investments

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:14.060
of an entire region.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.629
We don't need any kind of escalation.

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.965
What we need is peace.

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:19.665
And that's why

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.834
we proceed an open Balkan initiative.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:23.035
And that's why

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:24.504
we need to see, of course,

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:25.905
we have freedom of movement

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:26.772
and everything else,

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.608
and no one wants to see. Mr.

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:29.942
President, an escalation here.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:30.743
I don't think anyone's

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.211
calling for an escalation.

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:33.846
But let me let me just ask you this.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.014
Look, our colleague

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:36.949
kind of broke down for us.

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.151
What's at the heart of this?

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:42.321
And it's the fact that Serbia doesn't

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.723
recognize Kosovo

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.992
as an independent and sovereign nation.

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.159
What would it take, Mr.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.562
President, for Serbia to acknowledge

